nger":9469,"chroncontrolage":9508,"chroncontroltype":"Radiocarbon, calibrated"}]}}],"defaultchronology":11738},"sitedescription":"Glacial origin lake on Magerøya Island. The local bedrock is principally metamorphosed Late Proterozoic to Cambrian age sandstones, with quartzite, amphibolite and conglomerate layers. Site is located in tundra, a major component of which are dwarf-shrub communities dominated by Empetrum nigrum ssp. hermaphroditum, with Vaccinium vitis-idaea, V. uliginosum, V. myrtillus, and Betula nana as frequent and locally co-dominant components."}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}